Package: concordR
Title: Concordance-Aware Quality Control for Proteomic Interpretation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Artur", "Shvetcov", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "shvetsov1983@gmail.com")
Description: An atlas of RNA-protein concordance across human tissues,
    packaged as a quality-control layer for biofluid proteomic studies.
    Given a list of differentially abundant proteins from plasma or CSF,
    concordR evaluates whether each gene's nomination is defensible:
    whether its subcellular localisation is consistent with the sample
    compartment, whether it is expressed at protein level in the
    tissue relevant to the claim, and whether RNA reliably predicts
    protein for that gene. Built on an integrated atlas spanning
    488,190 observations across 11,154 genes, 24 tissues, and
    53 cell types.
